    "Microsoft_Expanded_Cloud_Logs_Implementation_Playbook_1737260229.pdf": {
      "status": "archived",
      "timestamp": 1775701378.354062,
      "model": "ollama/gemma4:latest",
      "moc_blurb": "This document outlines a critical shift in enterprise security: transitioning from basic compliance logging to advanced, intelligence-driven monitoring required to defend against nation-state attacks exploiting compromised user identities.\n\nThe core value is the ability to predict and forensically reconstruct sophisticated, stealthy attacks. Key findings highlight the significant technical uplift in Microsoft 365 logging, which now offers unprecedented granularity. Capabilities include capturing actual search queries, mapping specific data exfiltration instances, and monitoring API-level activity across SharePoint, Teams, and Exchange.\n\nSuccessful defense mandates integrating these deep logs into a SIEM platform (like Defender XDR). The operational focus must shift to behavioral profiling\u2014using techniques like `SessionId` correlation to build a cohesive attack timeline across services. Implementation requires specialized skills in data correlation, system integration, and mandatory budget allocation for the substantial increase in log storage and ingestion costs."
    },
